# This file is intentionally left empty.
# It's a common convention to use .gitkeep files to ensure that
# otherwise empty directories are tracked by Git.
# This 'models/' directory is intended to store 3D models for the WebAR application.
#
# For example, you might place .gltf, .glb, .obj, or other 3D model formats here.
# These models can then be referenced in the A-Frame scene (index.html)
# to be displayed in augmented reality.
#
# Example usage in A-Frame:
# <a-asset-item id="my-model" src="models/my-custom-model.glb"></a-asset-item>
# ...
# <a-marker preset="hiro">
#   <a-entity gltf-model="#my-model" scale="0.5 0.5 0.5"></a-entity>
# </a-marker>
#
# Remove this file if you add actual models to this directory and no longer need it
# to ensure the directory is tracked.
